    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day roll for the owner registration date already handled weekends but not public holidays. I extended `toBusinessDay` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set with the five fixed dates: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote the roll-forward logic as a loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed public holiday, so it lands on the next non-holiday business day.\n\nThis correctly handles chained cases too \u2014 e.g. Friday `2026-12-25` (holiday) rolls over the weekend to Monday `2026-12-28` (also a holiday) and finally to Tuesday `2026-12-29`. The implementation mirrors the reference algorithm the acceptance test uses, and `./mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
